 "day": 13,
 "topic": "Read receipts and delivery status",
 "tag": "CHAT",
 "script": {
  "hook": "Double ticks lie. Interviewers ask how read receipts really work.",
  "question": "Design read receipts and delivery status for a chat app.",
  "trap": "The trap: one boolean per message. It cannot tell sent from delivered from read, and it breaks in group chats.",
  "steps": [
   "Model the states. Sending, sent, delivered, read. A state only moves forward, never back.",
   "Ack at each hop. The server acks the send. The device acks delivery. The reader acks reading.",
   "Send a watermark. Send one read up to message ten, not one event per message.",
   "Handle groups and privacy. Store a watermark per member. Respect the receipts setting."
  ],
  "takeaway": "States only move forward, and a watermark beats a per message ack.",
  "teaser": "Tomorrow: local message storage and search.",
  "cta": "Comment M S D for the free cheatsheet."
 },
